{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794730838,"nonce":"zvSkJTNt8QWvBjBydpz4/jrmtlg=","message":"First cut in ~/Vibranium/hxnsl (local, not committed or pushed).\n\n- Front end: hlwgpu's HXSL at 9853fc8, package `hxnsl`, without its wgpu passthrough. hlwgpu's own copy is unchanged.\n- Tool `hxnsl \u003cshader.wgsl\u003e \u003cout dir\u003e [key=value ...]`: russl_compiler v0.3.2 (git tag; it is not on crates.io) through `compile_wgsl`, plus the bind group layout from naga 26, which compile_wgsl does not reflect. Writes shader.json and shader.spv.\n- A shader class gets WGSL, MSL + MSL_SLOTS, HLSL + HLSL_SLOTS, spirv(), GLSL_VERTEX/GLSL_FRAGMENT/GLSL_BINDINGS or GLSL_MISSING, LAYOUT and ENTRY_POINTS, beside HXSL's layout constants. `-D hxnsl_targets=` picks targets; `-D hxnsl_wgsl_only` skips the tool.\n- HXSL's `@const` is a WGSL override with no default, and russl's writers need every override fixed, so the class gives values with `@:constants({fog: true})`; the build fails naming any it leaves out. One value set per class: no permutations yet.\n\nChecked locally: cargo test (9), fmt, clippy -D warnings; the Haxe checks on --interp and on JS under node; the target defines; a @const without a value fails the build; an installed haxelib ZIP with the tool in bin/macos-aarch64 and no exec bit. spirv-val, glslangValidator and dxc accept every test shader's output. The Metal compiler did not run (no Metal toolchain here); CI's macOS job runs it.\n\nFor a Vulkan driver of hxn's own: russl writes SPIR-V with naga's default options, so ADJUST_COORDINATE_SPACE is on (Y flipped in the shader, where wgpu-hal flips the viewport instead) and FORCE_POINT_SIZE is off. Bounds checks are naga's defaults.","files":null}]}